Micha Pringle wrote:
>
> Anyone got some tips? I tried it with a huge heap of stuff (in a
> temple belonging to my God, thank goodness) and I ended up making a
> massive Clay Golem. What items should I polypile and what items should
> I avoid? Any other spoilers? Spoil me rotten.

Make several piles to reduce the issue, but it's a design feature that
items of the same material can merge to form a golem.  Kill it, spread
the items among the piles.  Except the chains from iron golems.  They
can't be polyed so carry them out of the pile and ditch them.

Avoid poly on: Any artifact whether you want it or not.  They resist
os if you have Trollbane stuff it in a chest.  Parts of your ascension
kit.  Gold and chains don't poly so don't bother.

Items that should be tossed in the polypile: Pretty much everything
else.  Take out the best items to keep for yourself.  Each shot, take
out the new good stuff and maybe put back the previous good stuff.
For example I'll always take out any silver dagger if my character can
get at least Basic in dagger.  But if my previous best dagger was a
stack of regular ones and a stack of elvish daggers appears, swap time.

